{
  "title": "Tomorrow",
  "title_target": "מָחָר",
  "goal": "Make plans and talk about what hasn't happened yet — the future tense, which marks the doer at the FRONT of the word, the reverse of the past.",
  "bekal": [
    "making plans and stating intentions",
    "using future-tense verbs",
    "saying \"don't\" with אַל"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "שִׂיחָה — תָּכְנִיּוֹת לְסוֹף הַשָּׁבוּעַ",
      "intro": "Thursday afternoon. Dana and Budi are making weekend plans.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "מָה תַּעֲשֶׂה בְּסוֹף הַשָּׁבוּעַ?",
          "baca": "mah ta'aseh besof hashavu'a?",
          "id": "What are you doing this weekend?",
          "literal": "what you-will-do in-the-end the-week?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "עוֹד לֹא יוֹדֵעַ. אוּלַי אֵלֵךְ לַמּוּזֵאוֹן.",
          "baca": "od lo yode'a. ulai elekh lamuze'on.",
          "id": "Don't know yet. Maybe the museum.",
          "literal": "still not know. maybe I-will-go to-the-museum."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "בּוֹא נֵלֵךְ יַחַד! אֲנִי אֶקַּח אוֹתְךָ.",
          "baca": "bo nelekh yakhad! ani ekakh otkha.",
          "id": "Let's go together! I'll pick you up.",
          "literal": "come we-will-go together! I I-will-take you."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "מְעֻלֶּה. בְּאֵיזוֹ שָׁעָה תָּבוֹאִי?",
          "baca": "me'uleh. be'eizo sha'ah tavo'i?",
          "id": "Great. What time are you coming?",
          "literal": "excellent. at-which hour you-will-come (f)?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "בְּעֶשֶׂר. אַל תִּשְׁכַּח לָקַחַת מַיִם.",
          "baca": "be'eser. al tishkakh lakakhat mayim.",
          "id": "At ten. Don't forget to bring water.",
          "literal": "at-ten. don't you-forget to-take water."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "לֹא אֶשְׁכַּח. וְאַחַר כָּךְ?",
          "baca": "lo eshkakh. ve'akhar kakh?",
          "id": "I won't. And after that?",
          "literal": "not I-will-forget. and-after-that?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "נֹאכַל בְּמִסְעָדָה עַל יַד הַיָּם.",
          "baca": "nokhal bemis'adah al yad hayam.",
          "id": "We'll eat at a restaurant by the sea.",
          "literal": "we-will-eat in-restaurant next-to the-sea."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "וּבַלַּיְלָה? יִהְיֶה מַשֶּׁהוּ?",
          "baca": "uvalaylah? yihyeh mashehu?",
          "id": "And in the evening? Anything on?",
          "literal": "and-in-the-evening? will-be something?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "יֵשׁ הוֹפָעָה. אִם תִּרְצֶה, נִקְנֶה כַּרְטִיסִים.",
          "baca": "yesh hofa'ah. im tirtseh, nikneh kartisim.",
          "id": "There's a show. If you want, we'll get tickets.",
          "literal": "there-is show. if you-will-want, we-will-buy tickets."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "כַּמָּה זֶה יַעֲלֶה?",
          "baca": "kamah zeh ya'aleh?",
          "id": "How much will it cost?",
          "literal": "how-much this will-rise?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "דָּנָה:",
          "text": "בְּעֵרֶךְ מֵאָה שֶׁקֶל. אֲנִי אֶבְדֹּק.",
          "baca": "be'erekh me'ah shekel. ani evdok.",
          "id": "About a hundred shekels. I'll check.",
          "literal": "about hundred shekel. I I-will-check."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "מְצֻיָּן. אָז נִתְרָאֶה בַּשַּׁבָּת!",
          "baca": "metsuyan. az nitra'eh bashabat!",
          "id": "Great. See you Saturday!",
          "literal": "great. so we-will-see-each-other on-saturday!"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "⚠️ **The future marks the doer at the FRONT of the word** — the exact opposite of the past, which marks it at the end. אֶ־ = I, תִּ־ = you & she, יִ־ = he, נִ־ = we. Once you've got these four prefixes, the whole future tense opens up.",
        "**One sentence to remember it: the past has a tail, the future has a head.** לָמַדְתִּי (I studied — tail ־תִּי) vs אֶלְמַד (I will study — head אֶ־).",
        "⚠️ **תִּ־ is used for \"you\" AND \"she\" at the same time.** תִּלְמַד can mean \"you (m) will study\" or \"she will study\". That's why the pronoun is often said in full: אַתָּה תִּלְמַד / הִיא תִּלְמַד.",
        "**Hebrew often uses the present for the near, settled future** — just like English \"I'm leaving tomorrow\". מָחָר אֲנִי נוֹסֵעַ לְחֵיפָה (\"tomorrow I'm going to Haifa\") is perfectly correct and far more common than the full future. The future tense is for what's uncertain, for intentions and for promises.",
        "**בּוֹא נֵלֵךְ** = \"let's go\". The pattern: בּוֹא (to m) or בּוֹאִי (to f) + the \"we\" future form. It's the standard way to suggest something in Hebrew, and you'll use it all the time.",
        "**אַל + future = \"don't\".** אַל תִּשְׁכַּח (don't forget), אַל תֵּלֵךְ (don't go), אַל תִּדְאַג (don't worry). Note it's not לֹא — לֹא תִּשְׁכַּח means \"you won't forget\", a statement, not an instruction.",
        "**אִם** (*im*) = \"if\". After אִם, Hebrew uses the **future** form: אִם תִּרְצֶה (if you want — literally \"if you will want\"). English uses the present here, so this is a small adjustment to remember.",
        "**נִתְרָאֶה** (\"we'll see each other\") is a warmer goodbye than לְהִתְרָאוֹת — and it's actually the same word, just as a sentence."
      ],
