          "after": [
            "⚠️ Notice that **\"you (f)\", \"you (pl)\" and \"they\" have a prefix AND a suffix** (־ִי or ־וּ). This is the only place in the future that uses both.",
            "Some verbs often break the pattern: לָלֶכֶת → אֵלֵךְ, תֵּלֵךְ, יֵלֵךְ, נֵלֵךְ; לָבוֹא → אָבוֹא, תָּבוֹא, יָבוֹא, נָבוֹא; לִהְיוֹת → אֶהְיֶה, תִּהְיֶה, יִהְיֶה, נִהְיֶה; לָתֵת → אֶתֵּן, תִּתֵּן, יִתֵּן, נִתֵּן. All four are among the most common verbs — memorize them whole, don't derive them from the pattern."
          ]
